---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const repo = "https://github.com/PilumRTS/pilum-releases";
// Direct installer URLs from the latest release's manifests; the script at the bottom refreshes them after a new release.
async function installer(os: string) {
  const manifest = await (await fetch(`${repo}/releases/latest/download/release-manifest-${os}.json`)).json();
  return `${repo}/releases/download/v${manifest.version}/${manifest.installer}`;
}
const mac = await installer("mac");
const windows = await installer("windows");
const youtube = "https://www.youtube.com/@PilumRTS";
const discord = "https://discord.gg/pv4KJVRcn3";
const email = "info@pilumrts.com";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---

<Layout
  title="Pilum: frontier colony RTS for Mac and Windows"
  description="Pump water, mine the rock, take what you can hold. Raiders come at night. Pilum is a tactical RTS of frontier colonies and war, in early alpha for Mac and Windows."
>
  <header class="topbar">
    <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Pilum, back to top">
      <span class="brand-mark" style={`--mask: url(${base}helmet-mask.png)`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="brand-name">PILUM</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#gameplay">Gameplay</a>
      <a href="#download">Download</a>
      <a href="#follow">Follow</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="helmet" style={`--mask: url(${base}helmet-mask.png)`} aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p class="kicker"><span class="tag">Early alpha</span> Build by day. Fight by night.</p>
        <h1 class="logo">PILUM</h1>
        <p class="headline">Every well you dig is a well you'll have to defend.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#download">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0-5-5m5 5 5-5M4 20h16" /></svg>
            Download the alpha
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={youtube} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z" class="fill" /></svg>
            Watch on YouTube
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Join the Discord
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="platforms">Mac and Windows</p>
      </div>
      <div class="horizon" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="about" class="section about">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="label"><span>01</span> The frontier</p>
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="lead">
            Pilum is a tactical RTS of frontier colonies and war. You're the commander sent to the edge: a landing pad,
            a dry plain, and settlers with nowhere else to go.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pump water from below the dust. Mine the rock for what it's worth. Trade with other outposts, and trust them
            as far as their guns reach. Every newcomer is a citizen, a worker or a rifle. You choose which, and you live
            with it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The raiders come at night. Rival outposts want your water, your minerals and the buildings you raised. Beyond
            the rim, something worse is watching.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nothing out here goes to waste. Knock out an enemy vehicle and it's yours to crew; lose one and it's theirs.
            Take a building without levelling it, move your own citizens in, and man it against the people who built it.
            Whatever you leave standing can change hands.
          </p>
          <p>Hold long enough and your forward operating base becomes a starport town. Then they send you past the rim.</p>
          <p class="note">Early alpha: features and visuals may change.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="gameplay" class="section gameplay">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="label"><span>02</span> Gameplay</p>
        <h2>Field manual</h2>
        <p class="legend">What is in the alpha today, and what is coming, marked <span class="soon">Planned</span>.</p>
        <div class="features">
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>The soldiers</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Every soldier is one man: he finds his own cover, returns fire, suppresses, and runs out of breath and ammunition.</li>
              <li>Spotting takes time. A man in the open is seen sooner than one lying still.</li>
              <li>Four kinds of squad: Assault, Support with machine guns and sentry guns, Engineers with rockets, mines and repairs, and Recon with a cloak, a sniper rifle, a drone and motion trackers.</li>
              <li>Grappling ropes up walls and onto the domed roofs.</li>
              <li>They call out contacts, kills and armour, over the radio when you're looking elsewhere.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>Wounds and loot</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Wounds land where the round did: a hit arm spoils his aim, a hit head slows his eyes, one bad leg and he jogs, two and he walks.</li>
              <li>No medics. Every squad carries its own medkits, and when they're gone, they're gone.</li>
              <li>Out of ammunition, out of kits? The dead don't need theirs. Strip any body for magazines, grenades, medkits and charges.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>Breach and clear</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>One click fights its way there; a double click rushes.</li>
              <li>C4 on the door, a grenade in the room, and the squad goes in.</li>
              <li>Smoke drifts with the wind. Weapons free, tight or hold. Break contact, support by fire, or stack orders and send them together.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>Armour and heavy weapons</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Battle tanks, and wheeled and tracked APCs with autocannons and rotary guns.</li>
              <li>Tanks run men down, ram through walls and shove wrecks aside. Engineers mend broken tracks under fire.</li>
              <li>Mortars, AT rockets, mines and sentry guns.</li>
              <li><span class="soon">Planned</span> A killing hit knocks a hull out instead of erasing it. Some burn, the rest lie there for whichever side's engineers reach them first.</li>
              <li><span class="soon">Planned</span> Any empty vehicle or gun pit can be boarded, the enemy's included.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>Nothing stays standing</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Walls and houses come down. Shells crater the ground and crack asphalt to gravel.</li>
              <li>Bridges break span by span. Fences and power lines fall.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>Night</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Moonlight, street lamps and lit windows. Shoot the lamps out, or bring the house down on them.</li>
              <li>Muzzle flashes give the shooter away. Headlights throw the soldiers' shadows.</li>
              <li>Fog of war: lost contacts fade to their last known position.</li>
              <li><span class="soon">Planned</span> A running day: build in the light, fight when it goes.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>The colony <span class="soon">Planned</span></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Wells on the aquifers, condensers that pull water from the air, solar by day and geothermal through the night.</li>
              <li>Hydroponics, quarries, an ore refinery and the mining rigs out on the open fields.</li>
              <li>Habs, a clinic, a cantina, an arsenal, a vehicle bay and, one day, a starport.</li>
              <li>Settlers come by ship when the place is worth it, and leave when the water runs out. Newcomers become Settlers, Citizens and Patricians.</li>
              <li>Soldiers are hired off the ship and paid by the minute. Walls, wire, gates, sentry guns, radar and bunkers keep the rest alive.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>Raids and rivals <span class="soon">Planned</span></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Growth brings the raiders. Two scouts at dusk, then the raid: they go for your warehouses, burn on the way out, and are gone by dawn.</li>
              <li>Clear their camps to take back what they carried off.</li>
              <li>Rival outposts want your water, your minerals and your buildings.</li>
              <li>Take a building standing: clear it, hold it, and send your own people in to run it. A bunker takes C4 on the door first. They can do the same to you.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card feature">
            <h3>With friends, or against them</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Up to four players, co-op against the AI or against each other, over LAN or by address.</li>
              <li>Seven missions: last man standing, body count, eliminate the commander, capture and hold, conquer, sabotage and retrieve.</li>
              <li>Generated maps from tiny to huge: rivers with bridges and fords, towns, walled compounds and houses you can fight through room by room.</li>
              <li><span class="soon">Planned</span> Write your own AI commander, and see if it beats ours.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Early alpha: features and visuals may change.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="download" class="section download">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="label"><span>03</span> Download</p>
        <h2>Ship out</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Mac</h3>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href={mac} data-download="mac">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0-5-5m5 5 5-5M4 20h16" /></svg>
              Download for Mac
            </a>
            <p class="small">
              The Mac build isn't notarized yet. On first launch, open System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security and
              click <strong>Open Anyway</strong>.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Windows</h3>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href={windows} data-download="windows">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0-5-5m5 5 5-5M4 20h16" /></svg>
              Download for Windows
            </a>
            <p class="small">
              SmartScreen may say “Windows protected your PC”. Click <strong>More info</strong> →
              <strong>Run anyway</strong>.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="follow" class="section follow">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="label"><span>04</span> Follow</p>
        <h2>Stay on the line</h2>
        <ul class="links">
          <li>
            <a href={youtube} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="link-kind">YouTube</span>
              <span class="link-value">@PilumRTS</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="link-kind">Discord</span>
              <span class="link-value">Pilum RTS</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>
              <span class="link-kind">Contact</span>
              <span class="link-value">{email}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span>© 2026 Pilum.</span>
      <span>Early alpha.</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    fetch("https://api.github.com/repos/PilumRTS/pilum-releases/releases/latest")
      .then((response) => response.json())
      .then((release) => {
        for (const asset of release.assets) {
          const os = asset.name.endsWith(".dmg") ? "mac" : asset.name.endsWith("-setup.exe") ? "windows" : null;
          if (!os) continue;
          for (const link of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>(`[data-download="${os}"]`)) {
            link.href = asset.browser_download_url;
          }
        }
      })
      .catch(() => {});
  </script>
</Layout>
